WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest
is an artist, actor,

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.335 size:78% position:39% line:92%
writer and filmmaker.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:05.638
Her movie "Kajillionaire"
is in select theaters now.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:06.272 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is where
the big one starts.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the noise,
it just keeps building

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:12.012 line:92%
and building and building.

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.513 size:88% position:44% line:92%
This one's not building.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.547 line:92%
The big one will be loud.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:17.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, if you're lucky,
you'll get crushed.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:21.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you'll -- you just di
right then and there.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Immediately.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.190 size:75% position:38% line:92%
A never-ending void.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.526 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow. So, YOLO.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:29.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome to the sho
Miranda July.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:31.097 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hello, Miranda.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.098 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hi there, Seth.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.266 line:92%
-I am so excited you're here

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.535
We've been trying to have you on
for a while.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I don't know if you remember

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:41.174 line:92%
We've actually met once before

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:44.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't think
that you would remember.

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:45.478 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No, I do, I do.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:51.851
You were -- So, you were
coming out of an elevator

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:55.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was going in,
and you turned.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you remember
what you said to me?

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not --
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:03.930 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You said, "I love you."

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:04.964 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And then the doors shut.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:09.803
Which a lot of people might have
taken the wrong way, right

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:14.074
Like, people might have though
you meant "I love your work"

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:21.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
or "you're so cool," but I kne
hat you meant "I love you.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.484 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I do.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.919 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.554 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I know.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:33.159
-So, uh, can we talk about
your movie "Kajillionaire"

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.794 line:92%
I thought it was fantastic

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:40.467 line:92%
It's a movie about, like, low --

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:44.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would say a lower-tier famil
of con men.

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:45.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that an accurate way
of describing it?

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, right,
not very good at their job

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:50.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not particularly good
and, you know, I know your wor

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:54.380
over the years and as we hav
established, I'm a fan of it

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's often autobiographica
to some degree.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:02:00.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is there any of you
in this family?

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.122 line:92%
Any of you in these characters

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you mean am I
a low-level con artist?

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:07.794
-Well, yeah, I mean, I guess
that's what I'm getting at

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.963 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.699 line:92%
-Well, I will say in the, like

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:16.836 size:84% position:42%
embarrassingly entitled
punk youth that I had,

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:25.311
there was sort of a cultur
of stealing and I did --

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
I stopped
and I don't condone that.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:30.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember, like,
a turning point for me was

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:35.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was, like, a guest artist,
visiting artist.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:35.722 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was 23.

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
I probably should have
been in college,

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.858 line:92%
not being a guest artist,

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:42.228 size:81% position:41%
but I remember kind of
scoping out the room,

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:46.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
as was my habit, for what
I could take on the way out.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.800 line:92%
Like, maybe a box of chalk

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
or that video projector
or something.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:54.240
And then, I caught myself
and I suddenly realized,

00:02:54.240 --> 00:03:00.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, you can either be thi
sort of respected artist perso

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:02.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
or you can have
the box of chalk."

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:03.316 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:06.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I guess I made
a choice there.

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, those were
your two paths.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:11.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we're certainly happy with
the one you picked.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've read that you got
this idea sort of half asleep,

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
the idea for this film,
and usually,

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would say most writers would
tell you the ideas they ge

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.968
when you're half asleep,
you wake up in the morning

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.970
and you realize it was not
a particularly good idea.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:28.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
How quickly did you know
that there was something here?

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.676 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Not very quickly.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:33.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just want to say that
for all the writers out there.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:34.914 line:92%
I had to withhold judgment

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:38.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it seemed
for the better part of a year,

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.620 line:92%
like, kind of a silly idea

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, these cons
and what does this all mean?

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.958 line:92%
Why waste my life on this?

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:47.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I got to the end
and read it back,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it kind of punched me
in the gut.

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.532 line:92%
And I guess at that moment

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:54.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Oh, maybe that is the movie

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:55.568 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Maybe that's the ride."

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you're laughing,
you're laughing,

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:58.404 line:92%
you're laughing, you're crying

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:01.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this is a film that -
I mean,

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:03.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
anxiety is a real theme
of this film,

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:08.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
not just the idea of an
earthquake, but also financial

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:10.850 line:92%
economic, and family anxiety

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:14.087
and it must be so strange
to have it come out at a time --

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:16.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
obviously, you made it
before all this happened -

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:20.994 line:92%
in this hot bed of anxiety now

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:22.328 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:22.996 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I know. It's so strange.

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:28.067
That anxiety was really personal
to me, and a lot of the themes

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:35.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
like the sensitivity to touc
and just the strangeness

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:36.075 line:92%
of this lead character --

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:39.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
Old Dolio is her name,
played by Evan Rachel Wood

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:45.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now, suddenly
those subtle themes

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:46.319 line:92%
are, like, front and center.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:48.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, those are not
my weird thing.

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:51.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's, like, the world's
weird thing now.

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:53.393 size:75% position:38% line:92%
We're all Old Dolio.

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:56.529
-I also want to congratulate you
on this monograph.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:59.232 size:88% position:44% line:92%
This is a book about you

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:03.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you had other people
basically contribute.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:08.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's like 80 peopl
that basically talk about you.

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:11.978
Was that terrifying to tur
over, sort of give the key

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:15.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
to families and friends
to tell your story?

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I think I thought
I would like that.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:22.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know how you secretly fear
that you're a narcissist?

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:26.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, like, you maybe take
the narcissist test online

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:27.026 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and you're like, "Am I?"

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:30.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I found out real quick
like, actually,

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:31.531 size:78% position:39% line:92%
it turns out I'm not.

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:35.335
Like, I hit my threshold
immediately and just had t

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:40.039
disassociate for most of the
experience of making that book

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:43.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
and pretend that everyone
was talking about somebody els

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:45.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was just maybe
working for that person,

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:47.880 size:88% position:44% line:92%
making her book for her.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.550
-It must be so strange too
because obviously people are

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:54.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
giving you materials,
and then, you have to --

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:56.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
because part of it is you take
yourself out of it, right,

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:58.391
and then you get this incredible
reflection of somebody.

00:05:58.391 --> 00:06:01.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I think sometimes with
autobiographies, you know,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.762
you're obviously getting
one person's perspective.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:05.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's so multi-layered
to have a bunch of people,

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:06.866 size:81% position:41%
but at the same time,
you're the gatekeeper.

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:09.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that a weird responsibilit
to have?

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:13.039
-I think I thought it woul
be more accurate that way.

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:17.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I was actually assigne
to write about myself,

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:20.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
and everything I started t
write didn't --

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:21.447 size:75% position:38% line:92%
it didn't seem true.

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:24.784
Everything was true, but i
didn't add up to the truth

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:25.485 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You know what I mean?

00:06:25.485 --> 00:06:27.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, even if
some of my friends'

00:06:27.587 --> 00:06:30.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
or collaborators' stories are,
like, a little off

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
or it's, like,
just their version,

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:36.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
somehow collectively,
it's more a life.

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:39.532
-It's really wonderful,
and one of my favorite --

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:43.736
before you go, I should say that
of the many things you've done

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:44.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of my favorite things
you ever did was

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:47.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
an interview with Rihanna,
I believe,

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
in "The New York Times"
back in 2015.

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:53.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I have long been
enamored with Rihanna.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:56.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that interview
was the first time

00:06:56.949 --> 00:07:00.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
I realized truly
how fun she was.

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:03.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that as much fun
to basically spend that time

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.591 line:92%
with her as it was to read

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:10.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I mean, we both are
drunk with Rihanna.

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:10.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:11.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
Although, she was
drunk with you,

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
whereas I think I was
the only one who would, like

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:18.471 line:92%
nervously drunk in myself.

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:22.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I -- Yeah, I mean,
she's just so lovely.

00:07:22.842 --> 00:07:23.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right?
-Yeah.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:27.213
-I'm so jealous that you reall
hung out with her like that.

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:30.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean, I'm just
so sad it's over.

00:07:30.183 --> 00:07:32.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's been over
for like over a year.

00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:33.186 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ] I know.

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:34.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm still just,
like, working through

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:37.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it's probably
not going to happen again.

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:40.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember her assistant --
like, I had to do

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
some last-minute fact checking
or something,

00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:47.200
and her assistant signed off
saying something like, you know,

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.768 line:92%
"See you around" or something.

00:07:48.768 --> 00:07:52.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for the whole, like,
next week, I was, like, ready.

00:07:52.572 --> 00:07:54.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, they were going to
call me to hang out.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-And I was like,

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:57.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
telling everyone, like,
"I don't know.

00:07:57.477 --> 00:07:59.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have pl-- you know,
she said, 'See you around.

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:02.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's -- you know, it'
probably in the next few days.

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:05.751
And then, someone pointed out,
like, that's just what people --

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:08.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's like, "Bye."
-Yeah, 'cause that was 2015.

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:13.059
I feel like those plans woul
have probably firmed up by now

00:08:13.059 --> 00:08:17.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, I guess --
Yeah, yeah, no, you're right

00:08:17.029 --> 00:08:20.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Miranda, it has been so lovel
to have you here.

00:08:20.099 --> 00:08:20.833 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The film is great.

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:22.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations
on the book as well,

00:08:22.735 --> 00:08:25.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I would like
to close the way we began,

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:27.807 size:78% position:39% line:92%
by saying I love you.

00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:30.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-[ Laughs ]

